		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=6588#p6588"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,<br />j&#039;aimerai bien savoir si la reponse de Marc Cousin marche chez vous car ça ne marche pas chez moi.j&#039;ai postgresql 8.1<br />voici l&#039;erreur renvoyé:</p><p>ERROR:&#160; syntax error at or near &quot;:&quot;<br />LINE 1: select * from recherche_mot WHERE recherche_mot:text ~ &#039;BARK...<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;^<br />To use type conversion operator (::) turn off the &#039;Allow using of parameters in query text&#039; option on Tools tab of Environment Options dialog or double colon symbols.</p>]]></content>
